  "text": "In September of 2018 we converged on the tax cuts. On September 28 fifty-nine of us said \"the tax cuts,\" fifty-eight said \"and small business,\" fifty-seven said \"tax reform 2 0,\" on the same day. Fifty-five of us said \"small business tax cuts,\" fifty-four \"and small business tax cuts,\" fifty-four \"cuts and jobs act.\" Fifty-three said \"tax cuts and\"; fifty-two said \"tax cuts and jobs act.\" Every one of these phrases peaked on that single day, September 28, 2018.\n\nThe record shows we did not originate these words. \"The tax cuts\" was first said by Bernard Sanders in 2017. \"And small business\" first appeared under Maxine Waters in 2013. \"Small business tax cuts\" traces first to Elizabeth Warren in 2017. We arrived at them later, together, and said them at once.",
